---
alwaysApply: true
---

- After editing a package, make sure all its tests and examples are passing.
- Keep code within the modality cli package as minimal as possible, refactoring code into other packages as needed.
- During development and testing, only build and use the debug `modal` binary, not the release `modal` binary.
- Use `modal killall` to killall running modal nodes during development and testing. Specify the --dir option to kill nodes in the current directory and its subdirectories.
- The Modal CLI is partitioned into domain crates under `rust/modality-cli-*`. When working on a specific command area, build only the relevant crate for faster iteration (e.g. `cargo build -p modality-cli-hub`, `cargo build -p modality-cli-net`). Build the full CLI with `cargo build -p modal` when integration testing.
- Domain crates use Cargo features for heavy optional deps. `modality-cli-contract` features: `p2p` (libp2p push/pull), `model-status` (modality-lang), `wasm` (wasmtime validation), `full` (all three). `modality-cli-program` feature: `wasm`. The `modal` binary enables `full` on contract and program crates automatically.